From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] rtsol: wait for an optimistic link-local address

xnu gives a new link-local address optimistic DAD (RFC 4429,
IN6_IFF_OPTIMISTIC). rtsol's interface_up() reports that as IFS_OPTIMISTIC,
which neither caller expects: the interface is taken to be down, and the
one-shot rtsol, finding every interface down, exits at once with status 0
without sending a solicitation. Treat it as tentative: wait for DAD to
finish (about a second), then solicit. Waiting, rather than soliciting with
the optimistic address, is what RFC 4429 asks of a solicitation that
carries a source link-layer address option, as rtsol's do. macOS doesn't
install rtsol (IPConfiguration solicits itself); NeoDarwin's netconfigd
runs it (docs/kernel/network.md, "P4-24").

--- a/rtsol.tproj/rtsold.c
+++ b/rtsol.tproj/rtsold.c
@@ -362,7 +362,7 @@
 	flags = interface_up(ifinfo->ifname);
 	if (flags == 0)
 		ifinfo->state = IFS_DELAY;
-	else if (flags == IFS_TENTATIVE)
+	else if (flags == IFS_TENTATIVE || flags == IFS_OPTIMISTIC)
 		ifinfo->state = IFS_TENTATIVE;
 	else
 		ifinfo->state = IFS_DOWN;
@@ -486,7 +486,7 @@
 				flags = interface_up(ifinfo->ifname);
 				if (flags == 0)
 					ifinfo->state = IFS_DELAY;
-				else if (flags == IFS_TENTATIVE)
+				else if (flags == IFS_TENTATIVE || flags == IFS_OPTIMISTIC)
 					ifinfo->state = IFS_TENTATIVE;
 				else
 					ifinfo->state = IFS_DOWN;
